    "body": "## Overview\n\nDraft, not for merge. A staging PR for vllm-project/ci-infra#825, so a scoped build can run its generator on a real GPU job.\n\n`entrypoints-integration-api-server` runs `PYTHONPATH=/vllm-workspace pytest ... entrypoints/serve/dev/rpc`. That `PYTHONPATH` replaces the one the shard setup exports, so pytest couldn't import the shard plugin. ci-infra#825 also copies the plugin into `python3`'s site-packages.\n\n## Claims\n\n- The step moves from 4 fixed pytest-shard jobs to `automatic_shard` (5 planned shards). The rpc command loses its `if` guard; the plugin runs it only in the shard holding its tests.\n- The AMD mirror isn't enrolled here and isn't in the scoped build.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Planned with ci-infra#825's generator against main's timings, and ran every shard's commands against a mock test tree: each test runs exactly once.\n- Scoped build with `VLLM_CI_BRANCH` set to ci-infra#825's branch, also covering three already-enrolled steps (`entrypoints-unit-tests`, `engine-1-gpu`, `amd-entrypoints-unit-tests`) as regression checks of the new setup line.\n\n## Details\n\nWill be closed after the build; the real enrollment follows once ci-infra#825 merges.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [ ] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n</details>\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
